WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.170
A prefix sum array stores cumulative totals from the start of the sequence.

00:00:05.170 --> 00:00:11.029
Padding with a leading zero aligns one-based prefixes cleanly with zero-based slices.

00:00:11.029 --> 00:00:14.200
Building the table takes a single linear pass.

00:00:14.467 --> 00:00:21.854
Any contiguous range sum equals the prefix up to the right boundary minus the prefix before the left boundary.

00:00:21.854 --> 00:00:25.883
Thousands of range sum queries finish in constant time each.

00:00:25.883 --> 00:00:29.107
Never rescan the slice when the array is static.

00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:32.832
A difference array is the inverse of a prefix sum.

00:00:32.832 --> 00:00:39.697
Adding a value to a range only touches the left endpoint and the index just past the right endpoint.

00:00:39.697 --> 00:00:44.571
After all updates finish, one prefix pass reconstructs the final array.

00:00:44.867 --> 00:00:50.272
Two-dimensional prefix sums accumulate rectangle totals using inclusion-exclusion.

00:00:50.272 --> 00:00:56.732
Add the top and left rectangles, subtract the double-counted corner, and include the current cell.

00:00:56.732 --> 00:01:00.358
Subgrid queries then run in four arithmetic operations.
